    {
      "id": "31beb6466aaf-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Which of the following cubes can be created by folding the given figure?",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Which of the following cubes can be created by folding the given figure?</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D31.png\" style=\"width: 161px; height: 66px;\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D32.png\" style=\"width: 88px; height: 73px;\" />"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D33.png\" style=\"width: 88px; height: 73px;\" />"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D34.png\" style=\"width: 88px; height: 73px;\" />"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D35.png\" style=\"width: 88px; height: 73px;\" />"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Opposite surface of the open dice can be find by below rules:-</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Alternate surface are opposite to each other.</li>\n\t<li>No two opposite surface are touched by side or by corners</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>So By using above rule we can find opposite surface of open dice.</p>\n\n<p>Below are the opposite surfaces:-</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D36.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 83px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D37.png\" style=\"width: 110px; height: 119px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>As we know that, no two opposite surface adjacent to each other.</p>\n\n<p>So in option 1, M and T are opposite surface but shown adjacent. Hence wrong.</p>\n\n<p>In option 2, P and S&nbsp;are opposite surface but shown adjacent. Hence wrong.</p>\n\n<p>In option 3, N&nbsp;and Q&nbsp;are opposite surface but shown adjacent. Hence wrong.</p>\n\n<p>In option 4, no opposite surface are adjacent.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, option 4 is correct.</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D31.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D32.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D33.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D34.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D35.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D36.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F1_Prashant_Madhu_27.11.20_D37.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
